text — the DEFAULT TYPE, and its manager is `edit`.

The type says what the content IS; the manager says what to do with it. `edit`
renders and edits the text, drives the status line, supplies the toolbar's
verbs, and gives meaning to Find, Edit and selection for a text file. It lives
HOST-side — CodeMirror here, Monaco or TextKit elsewhere — which is all that
"editing is the surface's" ever meant.

The type declares its STATIC verbs only. `Save` is not among them: emca emits
it while the buffer is dirty and withdraws it when clean, because its
appearance IS the dirty indicator (acme.c:383, with acme's Put translated).

Undo and Redo are here and nowhere else — available exactly where every
operation a window offers stays in a buffer emca holds.
